CAT = "cpabarRevenue"; SEG = "REV"
Q = [
("A company grants a customer a three-year license to its existing design software with no updates or other ongoing activities. Revenue for the license is recognized:",
 "At a point in time", ["Evenly over three years", "As the customer uses it", "When the term ends"],
 "Functional IP that the licensor does not change is a right to use, so revenue is recognized when control passes, at the start of the license period."),
("A franchisor licenses its brand name and supports the brand with ongoing advertising and activities that affect its value. The license revenue is recognized:",
 "Over the license period", ["When the license is signed", "When the franchise opens", "When cash is received"],
 "A license to symbolic IP is a right to access the IP as it exists through the term, so the performance obligation is satisfied over time."),
("A licensor of intellectual property receives a royalty of 5% of the licensee's sales. The royalty revenue is recognized:",
 "As the licensee's sales occur", ["When the license is granted", "Evenly over the license term", "When the year's sales are audited"],
 "The sales-based royalty exception in ASC 606 delays revenue until the later of the subsequent sale and the satisfaction of the related performance obligation."),
("A contract is modified to add distinct goods at their standalone selling price. The modification is accounted for as:",
 "A separate contract", ["A cumulative catch-up", "A change in estimate", "A cancelled contract"],
 "When added goods are distinct and priced at standalone selling price, ASC 606 treats the modification as a new contract and leaves the original contract unchanged."),
("A customer asks a manufacturer to hold finished goods it has bought until the customer has warehouse space. One requirement for recognizing revenue before shipment is that the goods are:",
 "Identified as the customer's", ["Insured by the customer", "Paid for in full", "Moved to a public warehouse"],
 "A bill-and-hold sale needs a substantive reason, goods identified as belonging to the customer, goods ready for transfer, and no ability for the seller to redirect them."),
("A retailer sells a separately priced extended warranty for $240 covering three years after the standard warranty ends. The warranty is:",
 "A separate service obligation", ["An assurance-type cost accrual", "Revenue when the goods ship", "A loss contingency"],
 "A warranty the customer can buy separately provides a service beyond assurance, so it is a performance obligation and its price is recognized over the coverage period."),
("A seller has a right to repurchase equipment it sold, at a price below the original selling price. The arrangement is accounted for as:",
 "A lease", ["A sale", "A financing", "A consignment"],
 "A call option at a repurchase price below the original price means the customer never obtains control, so it is a lease under ASC 842. A price at or above the original price is a financing."),
("Revenue analytics show revenue booked for orders with no record of customer approval. The step of the five-step model most in question is:",
 "Identifying the contract", ["Allocating the price", "Setting the price", "Finding the obligations"],
 "A contract exists only when the parties have approved it and are committed. Without approval there is no contract and no revenue to recognize."),
]
